==French==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|fr|bider|et}}. From {{m|fr|bider||to trot}}, of {{unk|fr|title=unknown}} ultimate origin. Possibly related to Medieval {{cog|it|bidetto||small horse}}<ref>{{R:it:Pianigiani|bidetto}}</ref>, itself probably related to {{cog|gem-pro|*bitiz}}<ref>{{R:MacBain|biteag}}</ref>; or, possibly from a lost {{der|fr|frm|rabider||go quickly, violently}}, a descendant of {{der|fr|la|rabidus||furious, fierce}}, with loss of the initial prefix.<ref>{{R:fr:TLFi}}</ref>

Modern sense derives from analogy with the straddling of a bidet and the straddling of a small horse.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

